    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #343\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nThe branch `bb/relay-213-implementation-audit-fixes-05-23-add-h-thr_wp66hj928i` has been pushed to origin and is confirmed to exist on GitHub (commit `992745b`).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #213: adds `heartbeat_occurrences` and floating next-fire scheduling.\n\n- New `heartbeat_occurrences` table (migration `0023`), one row per sweep-driven fire attempt, carrying the exact rule snapshot seen at enqueue time.\n- The sweep atomically inserts a `queued` occurrence and enqueues `{heartbeatId, occurrenceId}` under a distinct job key, idempotently no-op'ing on `(heartbeat_id, scheduled_for)` conflict.\n- `dailyTime`/`weekly` (fixed) rules advance `next_fire_at` immediately at sweep time; `interval`/`everyNDays` (floating) rules leave it `null` until the first fire attempt's actual start — fixing the delay-shifts-schedule bug.\n- The fire task now requires exactly one of `occurrenceId`/`itemId`/`triggeredByRunId` (rejecting violations as `validation_failed`), and the occurrence path locks the heartbeat+occurrence, cancels on disable/rule-edit via `jsonb` snapshot comparison, and lets retries reuse the persisted occurrence/timestamp without re-advancing the schedule.\n- Existing `onItemEvent` and manual (`heartbeat.trigger`) fire paths are unchanged.\n\nAll checks pass: unit (90/90), integration (678/678), e2e (5/5), lint, format, dependency boundaries, and full monorepo build.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
